   "blocked": "https://www.london.gov.uk/... returned HTTP 403 to an automated request on 2026-10-18; not retried or worked around. Figures below are as published by the GLA and quoted in web-search extracts of its pages on that date.",
   "rent_cap_initial": 0.0275,
   "notes": "Bromley is a London borough: shared ownership homes are marketed through Homes for Londoners and providers; the GLA caps the initial rent at 2.75% a year of the unsold share's value; household income up to GBP 90,000."
  },
  "london_living_rent": {
   "source_url": "https://www.london.gov.uk/programmes-strategies/housing-and-land/homes-londoners/london-living-rent",
   "checked": "2026-10-18",
   "fetched": false,
   "income_cap": 67000,
   "income_cap_note": "GLA material (July 2024) aligns London Living Rent with the GBP 67,000 maximum household income for intermediate rented products; older GLA pages still say GBP 60,000 - check the live GLA page.",
   "notes": "London Living Rent is an intermediate RENT product, not a sale: rents are set from GLA ward-level benchmarks at about one third of average local household income (adjusted by bedroom count), for working households who rent or live with others and cannot yet buy locally; it is meant to help them save a deposit (often to buy their home through shared ownership)."
  },
  "low_cost_rent": {
   "notes": "Low-Cost Rent (Social Rent / London Affordable Rent) homes are let by a registered provider to households nominated from the council's housing register (London Borough of Bromley). They are rented, not sold, so no purchase price applies."
  },
  "notes": "New-model shared ownership (homes funded from April 2021): buy 10%-75% of the full market value with a mortgage or savings and pay rent on the rest; all shared ownership homes are leasehold (service/estate charges apply). In this app, 'Intermediate' plots are treated as shared ownership: share price = share x market value; annual rent = rent_rate_on_unsold x (1 - share) x market value."
